{"case_id":"T5003","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["entry_point","API_protocol","state","input_semantics","attack_surface"],"confidence":100,"affected_functions":["spng_encode_image","spng_get_png_buffer","write_chunks_before_idat","write_idat_bytes","finish_idat","encode_row","encode_scanline","spng_set_text","spng_set_unknown_chunks"],"reason":"H0 exclusively fuzzes PNG decoding: it supplies attacker-controlled encoded bytes through spng_set_png_buffer, spng_set_png_stream, or spng_set_png_file and then calls decoding/getter APIs. S1 adds a distinct encoder workflow requiring constructed IHDR/chunk state, raw image data, spng_encode_image(), and post-encode ownership transfer through spng_get_png_buffer(); none of that protocol or its buffer-growth, compression, interlacing, chunk-serialization, and ownership behavior is exercised by H0.","evidence":["H0 calls spng_decoded_image_size(), spng_decode_image(), spng_decode_row(), and metadata getters, but never calls spng_encode_image() or spng_get_png_buffer().","spng_encode_image() consumes caller-controlled img, len, fmt, and flags after requiring ctx->stored.ihdr, creating a stateful API sequence absent from H0.","The new encoding path includes grow_buffer(), require_bytes(), write_data(), write_header(), finish_chunk(), write_idat_bytes(), and finish_idat(), exposing allocation growth, size arithmetic, pointer movement, compression, and chunk-length/CRC serialization.","write_chunks_before_idat() serializes numerous setter-controlled chunks, including text and unknown chunks; S1 activates substantive spng_set_text() behavior and adds spng_set_unknown_chunks().","encode_row() and encode_scanline() have separate interlaced and non-interlaced paths driven by ihdr.interlace_method, dimensions, bit depth, color type, and raw pixel layout.","spng_get_png_buffer() is only valid for encode-only contexts in SPNG_STATE_IEND and transfers output ownership via user_owns_out_png, a lifecycle/state surface H0 cannot reach."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated encoder fuzz target that derives valid and boundary IHDR values, raw image lengths/content, interlace settings, and optional metadata/unknown chunks from fuzz input; exercise valid and invalid setter orderings, call spng_encode_image(), retrieve output with spng_get_png_buffer(), decode the result for structural validation when encoding succeeds, and test context/output cleanup and ownership paths."}
